AI Document Assistant
=====================

Upload PDF, DOCX, or TXT files to build a knowledge base, then ask questions
about them by typing or speaking. Answers come from Google Gemini, grounded
only in the documents you've uploaded, with the source file (and page number,
for PDFs) shown under each answer.

Tech: React (Vite) + FastAPI + Axios + Google Gemini + LangChain + FAISS
      + pypdf + python-docx + browser Web Speech API

Pipeline: Upload -> Extract text -> Split into chunks -> Embed with Gemini
-> Store in a FAISS index on disk -> Retrieve the 3 most relevant chunks
for a question -> Send only those chunks to Gemini -> Answer + sources.

No database is used. The FAISS index and its manifest live under
backend/vectorstore/ and are rebuilt from your uploaded files if deleted -
uploads are not replaced by new ones, they accumulate into the same
knowledge base.


SETUP
-----

1. Add your Gemini API key

   Open backend/.env and replace the placeholder:

       GEMINI_API_KEY=your_real_key_here

   A free key can be created at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey


2. Start the backend (terminal 1, Windows)

   Requires Python 3.12 (pinned in backend/.python-version). Python 3.13
   is NOT supported yet - faster-whisper's ctranslate2 dependency ships
   a broken Windows wheel under 3.13 (its compiled extension is
   mislabeled cp313 but was actually built for cp312), which crashes
   voice input at startup. If you use pyenv-win, `pyenv local` in
   backend/ will pick up the pin automatically.

       rem 1. Install Python 3.12 if you don't have it
       rem    https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3120/

       rem 2. From the project root, create a fresh venv for the backend
       cd backend
       py -3.12 -m venv venv

       rem 3. Activate it
       venv\Scripts\activate

       rem 4. Install dependencies
       pip install -r requirements.txt

       rem 5. Run the server
       uvicorn main:app --reload

   Runs on http://127.0.0.1:8000

   venv/ and .env are both already excluded via .gitignore - never
   commit either one.


3. Start the frontend (terminal 2)

       cd frontend
       npm install
       npm run dev

   Runs on http://localhost:5173


HOW TO USE
----------

1. Open http://localhost:5173
2. Choose a PDF, DOCX, or TXT file and click Upload (repeat for more files -
   each one adds to the same knowledge base)
3. Click "Chat" in the top bar
4. Type a question, or click the microphone button and speak it
5. Click the speaker icon under any answer to hear it read aloud, or turn on
   "Auto Speak" to have every new answer read automatically


API
---

POST /upload
   Form data field: file
   Response: { "message": "...", "filename": "...", "characters": 1234, "chunks": 5 }

POST /chat
   Request:  { "question": "What is Machine Learning?" }
   Response: { "answer": "...", "sources": [{ "filename": "notes.pdf", "page": 2 }] }


NOTES
-----

- PDF, DOCX, and TXT are accepted. Old .doc files are not supported.
- Scanned PDFs with no text layer are rejected, because there is
  nothing to read without OCR.
- Each upload ADDS to the shared knowledge base. Re-uploading a file with
  the same name and content is a no-op (nothing is re-embedded). Re-uploading
  a file with the same name but changed content replaces just that file's
  chunks.
- There is no "remove a document" button. To reset the knowledge base,
  stop the backend and delete the backend/vectorstore/ folder.
- Chunking uses a 600-character chunk size with an 80-character overlap,
  and retrieval pulls the top 3 most relevant chunks per question.
  Change CHUNK_SIZE / CHUNK_OVERLAP / TOP_K in backend/services/rag_service.py.
- Voice input (microphone) and voice output (speaker / Auto Speak) run
  entirely in the browser via the Web Speech API - no audio is sent to the
  backend. They only work in browsers that support that API (Chrome/Edge).
  Unsupported browsers see the buttons disabled rather than a crash.

- Two separate Gemini models are used and both are set in backend/.env:
    GEMINI_MODEL           - generates the answer text
    GEMINI_EMBEDDING_MODEL - turns document chunks into vectors for search
  Their defaults ("gemini-flash-latest" and "models/gemini-embedding-001")
  were verified to work with a real key. If you ever see "model is not
  available for your key" for either one, list what your key can actually
  use:

      cd backend
      venv\Scripts\python.exe -c "import os;from dotenv import load_dotenv;from google import genai;load_dotenv();[print(m.name) for m in genai.Client(api_key=os.getenv('GEMINI_API_KEY')).models.list()]"
